22
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,650
But anyway, she is going to go with me.

23
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:39,010
So I'm going to drive down, pick her up.

24
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:42,720
And then we're going to drive all the way down together with her family.

25
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:47,360
And then go to the concert and spend the night!

26
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:58,660
We got tickets that are pretty much in the back, the nosebleed section. Cheapest tickets.

27
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:04,260
Actually, the cheapest and the tickets I got, I think it was like a $ 10 difference.

28
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,570
Hopefully Amy doesn't mind.

29
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,660
If not, I'll just pay for it.

30
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:15,330
Because it was a much better view between that $ 10. And I was like, it's just worth getting that better view.

31
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:17,860
So yeah, so we're, we have a decent view.

32
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:23,040
It's not like it's on the side or like at a weird or obstructed angle or anything,

33
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:27,390
but it, they were each 150.

34
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:33,500
I don't like how the ticket website advertised it.

35
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:42,870
They made it definitely seem that that was the price for two tickets. Not each ticket, even though I selected, I wanted to get two tickets.

36
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:48,640
But, but, Compared to what we paid in Korea for tickets,

37
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:52,980
how many years ago? Six years ago?

38
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:53,960
I was like, it's decent.

39
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:58,550
And when am I going to go again? So I got them.

40
00:02:58,550 --> 00:03:05,250
All the tickets now, it's like everyone buys them at once and then sells them, resells it.

41
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:07,440
